meta {
  name: Create Workflow Step
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/workflows/{{workflow_id}}/steps
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Notifier Maxime",
    "step_type": "notification",
    "order": 0,
    "configuration": {"channel": "email", "to": "maximejolivet.pro@gmail.com", "template": "nouvelle_demande_entretien"},
    "is_active": true
  }
}

docs {
  Custom controller (WorkflowStepsController), not API Platform's serializer
  -- unlike the rest of the API this one is snake_case: step_type, order,
  is_active. step_type must be one of: api_call, email, notification,
  data_transform, condition, delay, webhook, set_conversation.

  set_conversation only has an effect on the tool-calling path (it needs a
  Conversation in context, which manual/API triggers below don't have --
  it's a no-op there). Its `configuration.fields` maps a Conversation field
  name (visitor_first_name, visitor_last_name -- the only two supported) to
  an inputData key, e.g. {"fields": {"visitor_first_name": "first_name"}}.
  See docs/backend/SPECIFICATION.md §7.2.

  CAVEAT on the body above: WorkflowExecutionService::handleNotification()
  only ever reads `message`, `channel` and `webhook_url` from
  `configuration` -- `to`/`template` (as used here) are silently ignored,
  not a documented shorthand for "send an email using this template". With
  no `message` and no `webhook_url` set, this step is inert: it just logs
  an empty-message info line (`status: logged`) and notifies no one. To
  actually reach Maxime, either set `webhook_url` (POSTs `{"text":
  message, "channel": channel}` to a Slack/Discord/Mattermost-style
  incoming webhook) or use `step_type: email` instead, which does send a
  real message via Symfony Mailer.
}
